Hi all- I'm trying to run an ERGM on a friendship network of 41 nodes. I'm
looking at a number of individual differences (e.g., class, age, binge
eating) as predictors of friendship ties.

However, when I add in a structural variable like gwesp, gwdsp, or mutual,
it results in one or all of the variables showing no variability in the MLE
results. The standard error, MCMC %, and p-value for the variable(s) all
show NA.

One of the individual difference variables I'm using ("Class", which is an
ordinal categorical variable with 4 levels)  seems to be contributing to
the problem. When I remove that variable from the model, the model runs
even with gwesp included. However, Class is an important variable in my
analysis, and seems to be a strong predictor of friendship ties based on
earlier analyses, so I'd rather not simply omit it. Is there some reason
this particular variable would be breaking the analysis?

The model I'm trying to run, and the MLE output from this model, are below.
Thank you for any insight you can provide on this.


model4<- ergm(com ~ edges  + gwesp(alpha = 0, fixed=TRUE) +
nodematch("Class") + absdiff("Age") + nodecov("Age") +
absdiff("GlobalEDEQ") + nodecov("GlobalEDEQ") + absdiff("Binge") +
nodecov("Binge") + absdiff("BMI") + nodecov("BMI") + absdiff("TRIFINAL") +
nodecov("TRIFINAL"), control = control.ergm(MCMC.interval=20000) )

