Subject: [statnet_help] Long vector support for large networks
Message-ID: <CAGXqSMXQw9Kp4sqmPe8Q5WfHOFOak9soL3W3Zpg=K_SDzxqRBA@mail.gmail.com>

Dear listers,

I'm examining a series of 140 annual networks. In more recent years the
networks get very large (more than 27,000 nodes) and sparse (21,000 edges):

> netx
 Network attributes:
  vertices = 27123
  directed = FALSE
  hyper = FALSE
  loops = TRUE
  multiple = FALSE
  bipartite = FALSE
  total edges= 21570
    missing edges= 0
    non-missing edges= 21570

 Vertex attribute names:
    position club vertex.names

 Edge attribute names not shown

When I estimate an ERG model for such a large network, I run into the
following error:

> modelx <- ergm(netx ~ edges + edgecov(mg) + edgecov(m4) + edgecov(mt))
[1] "Warning:  This network is allowed to contain loops"
Error in ergm.getglobalstats(nw, model, response = response) :
  long vectors (argument 13) are not supported in .C

I believe this error message occurs because R is trying to pass a long
vector via .C, which doesn't support long vectors.

Did anyone else run into similar issues? If so, how did you engage with
this issue?

Any help is much appreciated. Thank you!

Best wishes,

Frank van der Wouden
University of California, Los Angeles
